@startuml dsd_uc1_makePayment
' NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram, UC1 Process Sale: makePayment(amount, tenderType) (Contract 4), W11
' Team D - editable source of assets/dsd_uc1_makePayment.png
' Reference for the payments of UC3 and UC5 (they use the same PaymentMethods, AD-08).
' Participants: logical view (architecture.md 4.2). Operations: system_interfaces.md 3.2, 4.1 to 4.3; AD-07, AD-08, AD-09.
title DSD UC1 Process Sale - makePayment(amount, tenderType) (Contract 4)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 8
skinparam BoxPadding 6
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBE6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B7791F
hide footbox
box "ui.api" #EAF2E3
  participant "ctrl:SaleController" as C
end box
box "application" #E8EEF7
  participant "h:SaleHandler" as H
  participant ":PaymentMethods" as PMS
  participant "pm:CreditCard\nPaymentMethod" as PM
end box
box "domain" #FFF7E0
  participant "s:Sale" as S
  participant "p:CreditCard\nPayment" as P
end box
box "application.interfaces" #F6EDF7
  participant ":CardReader" as CR
  participant ":PaymentService" as PAY
  participant ":Transaction\nRepository" as TR
  participant ":ReceiptPrinter" as PR
end box

[-> C : POST /api/sales/{saleID}/payment {tenderType: CREDIT_CARD, amount}
C -> H : makePayment(amount, CREDIT_CARD)
H -> S : canBePaid(amount, CREDIT_CARD)
note right of S : complete, no payment yet (BR-18),\ncard amount = total
S --> H : OK (else 409 / 422)
H -> PMS : get(CREDIT_CARD)
PMS --> H : pm
H -> PM : pay(s, amount)
PM -> CR : read()
alt ERROR: the card cannot be read (9b1a)
  CR --> PM : CardReadResult(ERROR)
  PM --> H : CARD_NOT_READ
  H --> C : CARD_NOT_READ
  C -->[ : 200 result CARD_NOT_READ: read the card again or another tender
  note over H : no Payment is created and the PaymentService is not called,\nso no voidAuthorization is needed; the sale stays open
else OK
CR --> PM : CardReadResult(OK, cardToken)
note right of CR : the card token stays in memory\nand goes only to the PaymentService (AD-09, DC-06)
PM -> PAY : authorize(PaymentRequest(s.transactionID, amount, cardToken))
note right of PAY : the adapter applies the 10 s timeout (AD-07);\nthe same transaction ID in every retry (IR-02)
alt APPROVED
  PAY --> PM : PaymentResult(APPROVED, authCode, reference, last4)
  PM -> TR : saveOpenAuthorization(s.transactionID, reference)
  note right of TR : IR-15: voided at start-up\nif the register stops before the save
  PM -> P ** : create(amount, authCode, reference, last4)
  PM -> S : setPayment(p)
  note right of S : isPaid = true
  PM --> H : APPROVED
  H -> S : reduceStock()
  note right of S : each SaleLineItem reduces\nthe stock level of its ProductDescription\n(below zero: recorded for FR-19)
  H -> S : createAccountingRecord()
  S --> H : record (with taxToBeCorrected)
  H -> TR : saveCompleted(s, record)
  note right of TR : ONE database transaction: sale, lines, payment,\nstock changes, AccountingQueue record and\nstore_sync_list entry; the open authorization is deleted (AD-05, DR-13)
  H -> S : getReceipt()
  S --> H : receipt (FR-71, last 4 digits only)
  H -> PR : print(receipt)
  PR --> H : READY (NO_PAPER: the sale is saved, reprint later, IR-13)
  H --> C : APPROVED, receiptNumber, last4, authCode
  C -->[ : 200 result APPROVED
else DECLINED (9b2a)
  PAY --> PM : PaymentResult(DECLINED, reason)
  PM --> H : DECLINED
  H --> C : DECLINED, reason
  C -->[ : 200 result DECLINED: another tender or cancel
else NOT_AVAILABLE: timeout or error (9b2b)
  PAY --> PM : PaymentResult(NOT_AVAILABLE)
  PM --> H : NOT_AVAILABLE
  H --> C : NOT_AVAILABLE (retry allowed)
  C -->[ : 200 result NOT_AVAILABLE: retry, another tender or cancel
  note over H : no Payment is created; the sale stays open with the same transaction ID.\nIf the cashier then uses another tender or cancels, the handler first calls\nPaymentService.voidAuthorization(transactionID) (AD-07, IR-15)
end
end

note over H, PM
  Cash and check use the same steps with CashPaymentMethod (amount tendered, change, cash drawer opens, IR-14)
  and CheckPaymentMethod (check number, authorization of the check, IR-16). Only pay() differs.
end note

note over H
  GRASP
  Polymorphism, Protected Variations: one PaymentMethod per tender behind a common interface (AD-08); a new tender changes no handler (NFR-09).
  Creator: the PaymentMethod creates the Payment it records (it has the authorization data).
  Information Expert: Sale reduces the stock of its lines and builds its receipt and its AccountingRecord.
  Pure Fabrication, Indirection: TransactionRepository, PaymentService, CardReader and ReceiptPrinter are interfaces (DC-02).
  Low Coupling: the controller only calls the handler; the handler never calls an adapter class directly.
end note
@enduml
